  "verification_notes": [
    "Map screenshots use explicit unlocked-map and cleared-enemy presentation fixtures; they are not natural campaign progress evidence.",
    "Nine-map graphical tests click actual route icons, approach, clear with progress and paid tools, climb through physical W input, and descend through mouse routing.",
    "Four graphical resolutions and fullscreen are covered, and the exported acceptance app additionally runs map clearance, routing and restore at four native resolutions.",
    "Four new real processes preserve partial clearance, complete it with one payment, resume a second-ladder climb, walk the return route and prevent duplicate settlement.",
    "Initial regression found surface rules applied to the legacy core scene without matching visuals. Terrain and clearing are now explicitly derived from campaign entry, and final related checks and binaries were rebuilt.",
    "Existing fixtures use the original core rules; the normal campaign, all new map tests and exported acceptance use the actual new environment rules.",
    "Normal exported Linux game additionally passed real OS movement, modal keys, search/return, close and restart.",
    "The cold-start probe now tolerates BadWindow only during startup tree enumeration; all target PID, real input, save and restart assertions remain required. An earlier probe attempt failed with X11 BadWindow during startup scanning before gameplay assertions.",
    "Final verification also covers equal-distance T return choosing the nearby opened landing, including a cross-process reload.",
    "All 58 recorded runtime source hashes match the clean regression copy and final export inputs."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Windows packages are exported from official Godot 4.6.3 templates; Windows hardware execution and PowerShell acceptance remain unverified.",
    "Actual audible sound requires a real audio device.",
    "Continuous exported desktop gameplay ran two minutes, not thirty; Linux software rendering is not a hardware performance benchmark.",
    "No new complete natural 35-day balance proof for surface delays and alternate routes.",
    "Maps still use two horizontal floors; this is not a fully procedural building or room navigation system.",
    "Public community descriptions guided independent design; no original-game native analysis or current-build numerical verification is claimed."
  ]
